      "title": "Man and police officer wounded in exchange of gunfire near Ontario synagogue",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/21/gunfire-belleville-ontario-synagogue-yom-kippur",
      "description": "<p>Officials say man was critically injured and officer was wounded in Yom Kippur incident near Belleville synagogue</p><p>A police officer and a man were wounded in an exchange of gunfire on Sunday near a synagogue in Ontario as members of the Jewish community marked Yom Kippur, authorities said. The man was hospitalized in life-threatening condition.</p><p>The Canadian province’s special investigations unit said the exchange of gunfire happened near the Sons of Jacob Synagogue in Belleville, Ontario, about 110 miles (160km) east of Toronto. Belleville police said the officer encountered the man at about 7.10pm and that both were taken to a hospital.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/21/gunfire-belleville-ontario-synagogue-yom-kippur\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-21T14:56:58"
    },
    {
      "title": "Police Officer Injured in Shooting Near Ontario Synagogue on Yom Kippur",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/21/world/canada/synagogue-shooting-belleville-ontario-yom-kippur.html",
      "description": "There was an exchange of gunfire near the Sons of Jacob Synagogue in Belleville as congregants gathered inside to mark Yom Kippur, the authorities said.",
